+def _closure(cfg: Config, d: Path, *, waves_of: Mapping[str, int],
+             paths: Mapping[str, Path], conflicts: Mapping[str, Collection[str]]) -> set[str]:
+    """The names of the bundles ``d`` was ordered after by a declared edge, transitively:
+    its in-run prerequisite closure (#463). ``waves_of`` maps each bundle of the run's
+    schedule to its wave; ``paths`` maps each in-run bundle — those, and the finished ids
+    the pre-wave carry carried (:func:`_carry_finished`, #646), which come before every
+    wave — to its directory. From ``d`` and each bundle reached, an edge is followed when
+    it is
+
+    * a plain ``Depends on`` or a legacy ``Stacks on``, to a bundle of either;
+    * a ``Depends on (merged)``, to a bundle of the schedule. One outside it waits for its
+      merge into the dependent's base (:func:`_runnable`, #186), so its work is on the
+      real base; one inside it is ordered before the dependent and merged nowhere;
+    * a ``Conflicts with`` (``conflicts``: either side declared it, among the run's live
+      bundles), to a bundle of the schedule in an earlier wave than the one it is
+      followed from.
+
+    Which of them have work to carry is :func:`_bundle_bases`' to judge."""
+    found: set[str] = set()
+    todo = [d]
+    while todo:
+        m = todo.pop()
+        bp = m / "brief.md"
+        edges: list[str] = []
+        if bp.exists():
+            edges += [n for n in (cfg.bundle(x).name
+                                  for x in brief.depends_on(bp) + brief.stacks_on(bp))
+                      if n in paths]
+            edges += [n for n in (cfg.bundle(x).name for x in brief.depends_on_merged(bp))
+                      if n in waves_of]
+        if m.name in waves_of:
+            edges += [n for n in conflicts.get(m.name, ())
+                      if n in waves_of and waves_of[n] < waves_of[m.name]]
+        for n in edges:
+            if n != d.name and n not in found:
+                found.add(n)
+                todo.append(paths[n])
+    return found
+
